						<a href="/#adventures">Travel</a>
						<a href="/#aviation">Aviation</a>
						<a href="/#food">Food</a>
					</aside>

					<div class="article-body">
						<p class="lead">Cassia’s conference was the reason we ended up in Toulouse. It brought us to a city that seems to live in two worlds—a center of modern aviation whose oldest streets, riverside views, and café tables invite you to slow down.</p>

						<p>Our week offered a little of both. Aviation was a natural place to begin. At Aeroscopia, historic aircraft tell the story of how flight evolved—and why Toulouse became so important to it. The Airbus tour carried that story into the present, offering a look at the immense scale and careful coordination behind the aircraft we see crossing the sky every day.</p>

						<div class="aviation-gallery">
							<figure>
								<img src="/images/aeroscopia-airbus-a340.jpeg" alt="Airbus A340-600 displayed outside Aeroscopia in Toulouse" />
								<figcaption>An Airbus A340-600 on display at Aeroscopia.</figcaption>
							</figure>
							<figure>
								<img src="/images/aeroscopia-airbus-beluga.jpeg" alt="Head-on view of an Airbus Beluga displayed at Aeroscopia" />
								<figcaption>Face to face with the unmistakable Airbus Beluga.</figcaption>
							</figure>
						</div>

						<section class="highlights" aria-label="Toulouse highlights">
							{highlights.map((highlight) => (
