									<span>{highlight.number}</span>
									<h2>{highlight.title}</h2>
									<p>{highlight.text}</p>
								</div>
							))}
						</section>

						<h2>Beyond the flight line</h2>
						<p>A riverboat ride on the Garonne changed the pace completely. From the water, the city’s bridges and warm brick façades took on a different character. It was a reminder that some places are best understood by stepping away from the streets for a while.</p>

						<figure>
							<img src="/images/toulouse-riverboat.jpeg" alt="Riverboat docked on the Garonne beneath the Pont Neuf in Toulouse" />
							<figcaption>Our riverboat waiting on the Garonne, with the Pont Neuf beyond.</figcaption>
						</figure>

						<p>Back on land, we explored the streets around the Capitole—the grand civic heart of Toulouse. The squares, shops, markets, and tucked-away corners made wandering as memorable as any scheduled stop.</p>

						<blockquote>In Toulouse, the journey moves easily from aircraft hangars to riverbanks—and there is always something worth tasting along the way.</blockquote>

						<h2>A city best explored slowly</h2>
						<p>And then there was the food: local markets, relaxed meals, regional flavors, and the kind of simple dishes that stay with you long after a trip ends. Toulouse gave us plenty to see, but the unhurried moments between destinations are what brought the week together.</p>

						<figure>
							<img src="/images/toulouse-market.jpeg" alt="Shoppers gathered around an outdoor market stall on a tree-lined square in Toulouse" />
							<figcaption>A neighborhood market—one of the everyday scenes that made Toulouse memorable.</figcaption>
						</figure>

						<p>It was aviation that first drew our attention to Toulouse. It was the river, the streets, and the food that made the city feel like more than a stop on the map.</p>

						<figure>
							<img src="/images/toulouse-sunrise-departure.jpeg" alt="Toulouse seen through an airplane window while departing at sunrise" />
							<figcaption>Flying out at sunrise, with Toulouse fading below us.</figcaption>
						</figure>

